abstract: >-
  Essence of INS Rana captures the glorious history,
  indomitable spirit, and operational legacy of one of the
  Indian Navy’s mightiest Rajput-class guided-missile
  destroyers. Blending vivid historical documentation with
  naval tradition and the proud heritage of Maharana Pratap,
  this book chronicles the ship's resolute, resilient, and
  relentless character, immortalising its role in shaping
  India’s maritime strength. It aims to establish a
  connection between the ship and the readers by reflecting
  upon its identity, signature, tenets, and glorious past.

  The book explores the unique ethos, valour, camaraderie
  and esprit de corps that define the ship’s legacy. It
  treats the ship's name itself as the subject, tracing the
  lineage of 'Rana' through successive warships and
  successive periods of naval service, from a First World
  War-era Royal Navy destroyer through later Royal Navy
  ships and two Indian Navy ships, up to the present INS
  Rana (D52). The book thoughtfully integrates the story of
  Maharana Pratap, enhancing its cultural and emotional
  depth.
